   371	/**Function*************************************************************
   372	
   373	  Synopsis    [Returns 1 if an stmap area-sensitive mode should reject a cut.]
   374	
   375	  Description [The area-sensitive guards are evaluated after matching the
   376	  candidate cut because their hypotheses need the candidate's actual mapper
   377	  area. In stmap6 exact-area recovery, a wide high-fanout cut is rejected only
   378	  when the existing match has slack and the candidate does not save at least
   379	  half an inverter area. In stmap7, the area-saving override additionally
   380	  requires more than two inverter delays of slack and excludes the highest
   381	  fanout-risk bucket. In stmap8, the override is further rejected when the
   382	  candidate match worsens mapper arrival by more than one quarter of an
   383	  inverter delay. In stmap9, middle-slack candidates can recover area only
   384	  when they are outside the highest fanout bucket, do not worsen mapper
   385	  arrival, and save at least one inverter area. In stmap10, that middle-slack
   386	  relief also requires the mapper node to be no deeper than level 96. In
   387	  stmap11, that depth window is tightened to level 64. In stmap12, the same
   388	  tight-depth relief is allowed only in the lower moderate fanout bucket.]
   389	
   390	  SideEffects []
   391	
   392	  SeeAlso     []
   393	
   394	***********************************************************************/
   395	static int Map_MatchSkipAreaSensitiveFanout( Map_Man_t * p, Map_Node_t * pNode, Map_Cut_t * pCut, int fPhase, Map_Match_t * pMatchBest, Map_Match_t * pMatch )
   396	{
